<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27787" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mămilla</span></b>  (incorrectly <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mamm-</span></b> ; cf. Lachm. ad Lucr. vol. 2, p. 36),
			ae, f.
		dim.
		mamma, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a breast, pap, nipple, teat</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Vell. 2,
				70, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 6, 400</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laeva in parte mamillae Nil salit juveni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 7,
					159</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scrofa triginta clara mamillis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					12, 74</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">13,
			163</span></i>.—As a term of endearment, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps.
				1, 2, 47</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a little pipe</i>
			joined to a larger one, <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 3, 14, 2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
